WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.233
Azure core services.

2
00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:07.339
Azure is the enterprise default wherever Microsoft contracts already exist.

3
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:09.133
Here's the efficient way in.

4
00:00:10.333 --> 00:00:10.921
Why Azure?

5
00:00:10.921 --> 00:00:16.267
Because the client's Active Directory, Office licenses, and procurement already live there.

6
00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:19.767
In India's services sector, that is very often the case.

7
00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:24.867
So the efficient way in is to map your AWS knowledge by analogy.

8
00:00:26.067 --> 00:00:27.067
Here is the map.

9
00:00:27.367 --> 00:00:29.700
EC2 becomes Virtual Machines.

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.533
Lambda becomes Functions.

11
00:00:31.833 --> 00:00:33.733
S3 becomes Blob Storage.

12
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.367
EKS becomes AKS, the enterprise workhorse.

13
00:00:37.667 --> 00:00:39.486
RDS becomes Azure Database.

14
00:00:39.486 --> 00:00:43.933
Same shapes, different names, and you learn the deltas on the job.

15
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.167
Azure has one organizing quirk.

16
00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:52.500
Everything lives inside a resource group, a named container for related resources.

17
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.060
Storage, clusters, and functions all sit inside it.

18
00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:59.767
You can tag it, secure it, and delete it as a single unit.

19
00:01:00.967 --> 00:01:02.933
Let's see it in the Azure command line.

20
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:06.867
First we create the resource group, in the Central India region.

21
00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.756
Then a storage account, inside that group.

22
00:01:09.756 --> 00:01:14.933
Where S3 had a bucket and a key, Azure has an account, a container, and a blob name.

23
00:01:15.233 --> 00:01:19.036
And a managed Kubernetes cluster, roughly the same as EKS.

24
00:01:19.036 --> 00:01:21.133
Note the group on every command.

25
00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:23.900
Here is the typical case.

26
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:29.373
A large client wants your ticket triage LLM system deployed on their cloud.

27
00:01:29.373 --> 00:01:33.167
It's Azure, decided years ago by a Microsoft agreement.

28
00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:37.533
Your Kubernetes manifests move to AKS nearly unchanged.

29
00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:42.699
S3 calls become Blob Storage calls, and the container doesn't care.

30
00:01:42.699 --> 00:01:45.749
Try mapping five AWS services from memory.

31
00:01:45.749 --> 00:01:48.000
That mapping is the onboarding.

32
00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.000
Let's recap.

33
00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.267
Azure is the enterprise default where Microsoft contracts exist.

34
00:01:54.567 --> 00:01:58.833
Map your AWS knowledge by analogy, then learn the differences.

35
00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.333
Everything lives inside a resource group.

36
00:02:01.633 --> 00:02:04.092
The concepts transfer one to one.

37
00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:05.433
Next up: Azure AI.
